{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QFUh2MmKQoMeUAdzBQrUEc","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import { actions } from 'astro:actions';\n     2→import { useActionState } from 'react';\n     3→import { useFormStatus } from 'react-dom';\n     4→import { withState } from '@astrojs/react/actions';\n     5→\n     6→export function Like({ postId, label, likes }: { postId: string; label: string; likes: number }) {\n     7→\treturn (\n     8→\t\t<form action={actions.blog.like}>\n     9→\t\t\t<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"postId\" value={postId} />\n    10→\t\t\t<Button likes={likes} label={label} />\n    11→\t\t</form>\n    12→\t);\n    13→}\n    14→\n    15→\n    16→export function LikeWithActionState({ postId, label, likes: initial }: { postId: string; label: string; likes: number }) {\n    17→\tconst [likes, action] = useActionState(\n    18→\t\twithState(actions.blog.likeWithActionState),\n    19→\t\t{ data: initial },\n    20→\t);\n    21→\n    22→\treturn (\n    23→\t\t<form action={action}>\n    24→\t\t\t<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"postId\" value={postId} />\n    25→\t\t\t<Button likes={likes.data} label={label} />\n    26→\t\t</form>\n    27→\t);\n    28→}\n    29→\n    30→function Button({likes, label}: {likes: number; label: string}) {\n    31→\tconst { pending } = useFormStatus();\n    32→\n    33→\treturn (\n    34→\t\t<button aria-label={label} disabled={pending} type=\"submit\">\n    35→\t\t\t{likes} ❤️\n    36→\t\t</button>\n    37→\t)\n    38→}\n    39→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018cewbrAQTiCboLWeF2v3xv","session_id":"7e54f64e-01ee-4d8c-b9c5-40d315771686","uuid":"5b9ef