{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018cewbrAQTiCboLWeF2v3xv","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information. Let me create a comprehensive report:\n\n## React Patterns Analysis Report - Astro Reference Project\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the Astro reference project to understand React patterns. Here are the key findings:\n\n### 1. **Component Mounting/Unmounting Patterns**\n\n#### Modern React (React 18+) - `client.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { createRoot, hydrateRoot, type Root } from 'react-dom/client';\n\n// Root caching for re-renders\nlet rootMap = new WeakMap<HTMLElement, Root>();\nconst getOrCreateRoot = (element: HTMLElement, creator: () => Root) => {\n  let root = rootMap.get(element);\n  if (!root) {\n    root = creator();\n    rootMap.set(element, root);\n  }\n  return root;\n};\n\nexport default (element: HTMLElement) =>\n  (\n    Component: any,\n    props: Record<string, any>,\n    { default: children, ...slotted }: Record<string, any>,\n    { client }: Record<string, string},\n  ) => {\n    if (!element.hasAttribute('ssr')) return;\n\n    const componentEl = createElement(Component, props, getChildren(children, ...));\n    \n    if (client === 'only') {\n      // Pure client-side rendering\n      return startTransition(() => {\n        const root = getOrCreateRoot(element, () => {\n          const r = createRoot(element);\n          element.addEventListener('astro:unmount', () => r.unmount(), { once: true });\n          return r;\n        });\n        root.render(componentEl);\n      });\n    }\n    \n    // Server-side rendered hydration\n    startTransition(() => {\n      const root = getOrCreateRoot(element, () => {\n        const r = hydrateRoot(element, componentEl, renderOptions as any);\n        element.addEventListener('astro:unmount', () => r.unmount(), { once: true });\n        return r;\n      });\n      root.render(componentEl);\n    });\n  };\n```\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Uses `createRoot()` for client-only rendering\n- Uses `hydrateRoot()` for hydration (SSR+client)\n- Maintains a `WeakMap` of roots per element to enable re-renders\n- Wraps in `startTransition()` for React 18+ concurrent features\n- Listens for `astro:unmount` event for cleanup\n\n#### Legacy React 17 - `client-v17.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { hydrate, render, unmountComponentAtNode } from 'react-dom';\n\nexport default (element: HTMLElement) =>\n  (Component: any, props: Record<string, any>, { default: children, ...slotted }, { client }) => {\n    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(slotted)) {\n      props[key] = createElement(StaticHtml, { value, name: key });\n    }\n    const componentEl = createElement(Component, props, children != null ? createElement(StaticHtml, { value: children }) : children);\n\n    const isHydrate = client !== 'only';\n    const bootstrap = isHydrate ? hydrate : render;\n    bootstrap(componentEl, element);\n    element.addEventListener('astro:unmount', () => unmountComponentAtNode(element), { once: true });\n  };\n```\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Uses `render()` for client-only, `hydrate()` for hydration\n- Uses `unmountComponentAtNode()` for cleanup\n- No root caching needed (older React API)\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Props Handling and Updates**\n\nProps flow through several stages:\n\n#### Server-side Processing (`server.ts`)\n```typescript\nasync function renderToStaticMarkup(\n  this: RendererContext,\n  Component: any,\n  props: Record<string, any>,\n  { default: children, ...slotted }: Record<string, any>,\n  metadata?: AstroComponentMetadata,\n) {\n  // Process slotted props (named slots)\n  const slots: Record<string, any> = {};\n  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(slotted)) {\n    const name = slotName(key);\n    slots[name] = React.createElement(StaticHtml, {\n      hydrate: needsHydration(metadata),\n      value,\n      name,\n    });\n  }\n  \n  // Merge slots into props\n  const newProps = {\n    ...props,\n    ...slots,\n  };\n  \n  // Handle children\n  const newChildren = children ?? props.children;\n  if (children && opts.experimentalReactChildren) {\n    attrs['data-react-children'] = true;\n    const convert = await import('./vnode-children.js').then((mod) => mod.default);\n    newProps.children = convert(children);\n  } else if (newChildren != null) {\n    newProps.children = React.createElement(StaticHtml, {\n      hydrate: needsHydration(metadata),\n      value: newChildren,\n    });\n  }\n  \n  const vnode = React.createElement(Component, newProps);\n  // SSR render to HTML string\n  const html = await ReactDOM.renderToReadableStream(vnode, renderOptions);\n  return { html, attrs };\n}\n```\n\n#### Client-side Props Reconstruction (`client.ts`)\n```typescript\n// Props come as plain objects from DOM attributes\nconst props: Record<string, any> = {}; // Passed in as arg\nconst children: string = element.getAttribute('...'); // From DOM\n\n// Create React element with props\nconst componentEl = createElement(\n  Component,\n  props,                    // Plain object props\n  getChildren(children, ...) // Processed children\n);\n\n// Re-render updates: root.render() is called again with updated props\n// React diffs the vnode and updates only changed parts\nroot.render(componentEl);\n```\n\n**Props Flow:**\n1. Server renders component with props → HTML attributes\n2. HTML sent to client with attributes containing props\n3. Client parses attributes, creates React element with props\n4. On updates, component re-rendered with new props via `root.render()`\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Slots/Children Handling**\n\n#### StaticHtml Component (Wrapper for HTML content)\n```typescript\n// static-html.ts\nconst StaticHtml = ({\n  value,      // HTML string from server\n  name,       // Slot name\n  hydrate = true,\n}: {\n  value: string | null;\n  name?: string;\n  hydrate?: boolean;\n}) => {\n  if (!value) return null;\n  const tagName = hydrate ? 'astro-slot' : 'astro-static-slot';\n  return h(tagName, {\n    name,\n    suppressHydrationWarning: true,\n    dangerouslySetInnerHTML: { __html: value },\n  });\n};\n\n// Prevent React from re-rendering children\nStaticHtml.shouldComponentUpdate = () => false;\n```\n\n#### Named Slots as Props\n```typescript\n// In server.ts - named slots become props\nfor (const [key, value] of Object.entries(slotted)) {\n  const name = slotName(key); // \"my-slot\" → \"mySlot\"\n  slots[name] = React.createElement(StaticHtml, { value, name });\n}\nconst newProps = { ...props, ...slots }; // slots are props!\n```\n\n#### Default Slot as Children\n```typescript\n// In client.ts\nfunction getChildren(childString: string, experimentalReactChildren: boolean) {\n  if (experimentalReactChildren && childString) {\n    // Advanced: parse HTML children into React vnodes\n    let template = document.createElement('template');\n    template.innerHTML = childString;\n    return Array.from(template.content.children).map(createReactElementFromDOMElement);\n  } else if (childString) {\n    // Default: wrap in StaticHtml\n    return createElement(StaticHtml, { value: childString });\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n\nconst componentEl = createElement(\n  Component,\n  props,\n  getChildren(children, element.hasAttribute('data-react-children')),\n);\n```\n\n#### Example Component Usage\n```typescript\n// Counter.tsx\nexport default function Counter({\n  children,\n  count: initialCount,\n}: {\n  children: JSX.Element;\n  count: number;\n}) {\n  const [count, setCount] = useState(initialCount);\n  return (\n    <>\n      <div className=\"counter\">\n        <button onClick={() => setCount(i => i + 1)}>+</button>\n        <pre>{count}</pre>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"counter-message\">{children}</div>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n\n// Component with conditional children\nexport default function Parent({ children }) {\n  const [show, setShow] = useState(false);\n  \n  return (\n    <>\n      <input onChange={() => setShow(!show)} />\n      {show ? children : 'Nothing'}\n    </>\n  );\n}\n\n// Fragment wrapper for children passthrough\nexport default function PassesChildren({ children }) {\n  return <Fragment>{ children }</Fragment>;\n}\n```\n\n**Key Insight:** Slots flow as HTML strings from the server, wrapped in `StaticHtml` components. This prevents React from re-rendering static content (performance optimization via `shouldComponentUpdate = () => false`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. **State Management and Reactivity**\n\n#### useState (Built-in React Hooks)\n```typescript\nexport default function Counter({ count: initialCount }) {\n  const [count, setCount] = useState(initialCount);\n  const add = () => setCount((i) => i + 1);\n  const subtract = () => setCount((i) => i - 1);\n  \n  return (\n    <>\n      <button onClick={subtract}>-</button>\n      <pre>{count}</pre>\n      <button onClick={add}>+</button>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n#### Nanostores (Global Signal-like Store)\n```typescript\n// cartStore.ts\nimport { atom, map } from 'nanostores';\n\nexport const isCartOpen = atom(false);\nexport const cartItems = map<Record<string, CartItem>>({});\n\nexport function addCartItem({ id, name, imageSrc }: CartItemDisplayInfo) {\n  const existingEntry = cartItems.get()[id];\n  if (existingEntry) {\n    cartItems.setKey(id, { ...existingEntry, quantity: existingEntry.quantity + 1 });\n  } else {\n    cartItems.setKey(id, { id, name, imageSrc, quantity: 1 });\n  }\n}\n\n// CartFlyoutToggle.tsx - subscribe to store\nexport default function CartFlyoutToggle() {\n  const $isCartOpen = useStore(isCartOpen);\n  return <button onClick={() => isCartOpen.set(!$isCartOpen)}>Cart</button>;\n}\n\n// CartFlyout.tsx - derive from store\nexport default function CartFlyout() {\n  const $isCartOpen = useStore(isCartOpen);\n  const $cartItems = useStore(cartItems);\n  \n  return (\n    <aside hidden={!$isCartOpen}>\n      {Object.values($cartItems).map((cartItem) => (\n        <li key={cartItem.id}>\n          <img src={cartItem.imageSrc} alt={cartItem.name} />\n          <h3>{cartItem.name}</h3>\n          <p>Quantity: {cartItem.quantity}</p>\n        </li>\n      ))}\n    </aside>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n#### Server Actions with useActionState (React 19)\n```typescript\nimport { actions } from 'astro:actions';\nimport { useActionState } from 'react';\nimport { useFormStatus } from 'react-dom';\nimport { withState } from '@astrojs/react/actions';\n\nexport function LikeWithActionState({ postId, label, likes: initial }) {\n  const [likes, action] = useActionState(\n    withState(actions.blog.likeWithActionState),\n    { data: initial },\n  );\n\n  return (\n    <form action={action}>\n      <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"postId\" value={postId} />\n      <Button likes={likes.data} label={label} />\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction Button({likes, label}) {\n  const { pending } = useFormStatus();\n  return (\n    <button disabled={pending} type=\"submit\">\n      {likes} ❤️\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**State Patterns:**\n- **Local:** `useState()` for component state\n- **Global (Signals):** Nanostores (`atom()`, `map()`) for cross-component state\n- **Server State:** Server actions with `useActionState()` for form submissions\n\n---\n\n### 5. **SSR and Hydration Flow**\n\n#### Server-side Rendering\n```typescript\n// server.ts - Renders to HTML\nasync function renderToStaticMarkup(Component, props, { default: children, ...slotted }) {\n  const newProps = { ...props, ...slots };\n  const vnode = React.createElement(Component, newProps);\n  \n  // Choose streaming or non-streaming\n  if (opts.experimentalDisableStreaming) {\n    html = ReactDOM.renderToString(vnode); // Blocking\n  } else if ('renderToReadableStream' in ReactDOM) {\n    html = await renderToReadableStreamAsync(vnode, renderOptions); // Streaming (modern)\n  } else {\n    html = await renderToPipeableStreamAsync(vnode, renderOptions); // Streaming (legacy)\n  }\n  \n  return { html, attrs }; // HTML + props for hydration\n}\n```\n\n#### Hydration Options\n```typescript\n// client.ts\nconst renderOptions = {\n  identifierPrefix: element.getAttribute('prefix'),\n  formState,\n};\n\nconst r = hydrateRoot(element, componentEl, renderOptions as any);\n```\n\n#### Form State Preservation\n```typescript\n// Actions responses are passed via data attributes\nconst formState =\n  actionKey && actionName && stringifiedActionResult\n    ? [JSON.parse(stringifiedActionResult), actionKey, actionName]\n    : undefined;\n\n// Passed to hydrateRoot for React 19 form integration\nconst renderOptions = { formState };\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Aspect | Pattern | Technology |\n|--------|---------|------------|\n| **Mounting** | createRoot/hydrateRoot (React 18) | React DOM Client API |\n| **Props Flow** | Server attrs → Client parse → React element | Plain objects |\n| **Slots (Named)** | Props with StaticHtml wrapper | React components |\n| **Slots (Default)** | Children prop with StaticHtml | React.createElement |\n| **Local State** | useState hook | React Hooks |\n| **Global State** | atom/map signals | Nanostores |\n| **Server State** | useActionState + actions | React 19 APIs |\n| **SSR** | renderToReadableStream | React DOM Server |\n| **Unmounting** | astro:unmount event listener | Custom event |\n| **Re-renders** | root.render() with new props | Root caching (WeakMap) |\n\n---\n\n### Absolute File Paths (Reference)\n\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/client.ts` - Modern React mounting\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/client-v17.ts` - Legacy React mounting\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/server.ts` - SSR implementation\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/static-html.ts` - Slot wrapper component\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/vnode-children.ts` - Children parsing utility\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/examples/with-nanostores/src/cartStore.ts` - Global state example\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/examples/framework-react/src/components/Counter.tsx` - Component example"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aeff186 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 41430\ntool_uses: 24\nduration_ms: 49598</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e54f64e-01ee-4d8c-b9c5-40d315771686","uuid":"64225c84-3754-46c7-8470-cf60d1ac1fe8","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand patterns from the reference React/Astro project at /home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro. Specifically:\n\n1. How React components are mounted/unmounted (look for createRoot, hydrateRoot, ReactDOM patterns)\n2. How props are passed and updated for React components\n3. How slots/children are handled in React within this project\n4. Any signal/store patterns used for reactive state management\n\nSearch the project thoroughly and report your findings with relevant code snippets.","agentId":"aeff186","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information. Let me create a comprehensive report:\n\n## React Patterns Analysis Report - Astro Reference Project\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the Astro reference project to understand React patterns. Here are the key findings:\n\n### 1. **Component Mounting/Unmounting Patterns**\n\n#### Modern React (React 18+) - `client.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { createRoot, hydrateRoot, type Root } from 'react-dom/client';\n\n// Root caching for re-renders\nlet rootMap = new WeakMap<HTMLElement, Root>();\nconst getOrCreateRoot = (element: HTMLElement, creator: () => Root) => {\n  let root = rootMap.get(element);\n  if (!root) {\n    root = creator();\n    rootMap.set(element, root);\n  }\n  return root;\n};\n\nexport default (element: HTMLElement) =>\n  (\n    Component: any,\n    props: Record<string, any>,\n    { default: children, ...slotted }: Record<string, any>,\n    { client }: Record<string, string},\n  ) => {\n    if (!element.hasAttribute('ssr')) return;\n\n    const componentEl = createElement(Component, props, getChildren(children, ...));\n    \n    if (client === 'only') {\n      // Pure client-side rendering\n      return startTransition(() => {\n        const root = getOrCreateRoot(element, () => {\n          const r = createRoot(element);\n          element.addEventListener('astro:unmount', () => r.unmount(), { once: true });\n          return r;\n        });\n        root.render(componentEl);\n      });\n    }\n    \n    // Server-side rendered hydration\n    startTransition(() => {\n      const root = getOrCreateRoot(element, () => {\n        const r = hydrateRoot(element, componentEl, renderOptions as any);\n        element.addEventListener('astro:unmount', () => r.unmount(), { once: true });\n        return r;\n      });\n      root.render(componentEl);\n    });\n  };\n```\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Uses `createRoot()` for client-only rendering\n- Uses `hydrateRoot()` for hydration (SSR+client)\n- Maintains a `WeakMap` of roots per element to enable re-renders\n- Wraps in `startTransition()` for React 18+ concurrent features\n- Listens for `astro:unmount` event for cleanup\n\n#### Legacy React 17 - `client-v17.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { hydrate, render, unmountComponentAtNode } from 'react-dom';\n\nexport default (element: HTMLElement) =>\n  (Component: any, props: Record<string, any>, { default: children, ...slotted }, { client }) => {\n    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(slotted)) {\n      props[key] = createElement(StaticHtml, { value, name: key });\n    }\n    const componentEl = createElement(Component, props, children != null ? createElement(StaticHtml, { value: children }) : children);\n\n    const isHydrate = client !== 'only';\n    const bootstrap = isHydrate ? hydrate : render;\n    bootstrap(componentEl, element);\n    element.addEventListener('astro:unmount', () => unmountComponentAtNode(element), { once: true });\n  };\n```\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Uses `render()` for client-only, `hydrate()` for hydration\n- Uses `unmountComponentAtNode()` for cleanup\n- No root caching needed (older React API)\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Props Handling and Updates**\n\nProps flow through several stages:\n\n#### Server-side Processing (`server.ts`)\n```typescript\nasync function renderToStaticMarkup(\n  this: RendererContext,\n  Component: any,\n  props: Record<string, any>,\n  { default: children, ...slotted }: Record<string, any>,\n  metadata?: AstroComponentMetadata,\n) {\n  // Process slotted props (named slots)\n  const slots: Record<string, any> = {};\n  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(slotted)) {\n    const name = slotName(key);\n    slots[name] = React.createElement(StaticHtml, {\n      hydrate: needsHydration(metadata),\n      value,\n      name,\n    });\n  }\n  \n  // Merge slots into props\n  const newProps = {\n    ...props,\n    ...slots,\n  };\n  \n  // Handle children\n  const newChildren = children ?? props.children;\n  if (children && opts.experimentalReactChildren) {\n    attrs['data-react-children'] = true;\n    const convert = await import('./vnode-children.js').then((mod) => mod.default);\n    newProps.children = convert(children);\n  } else if (newChildren != null) {\n    newProps.children = React.createElement(StaticHtml, {\n      hydrate: needsHydration(metadata),\n      value: newChildren,\n    });\n  }\n  \n  const vnode = React.createElement(Component, newProps);\n  // SSR render to HTML string\n  const html = await ReactDOM.renderToReadableStream(vnode, renderOptions);\n  return { html, attrs };\n}\n```\n\n#### Client-side Props Reconstruction (`client.ts`)\n```typescript\n// Props come as plain objects from DOM attributes\nconst props: Record<string, any> = {}; // Passed in as arg\nconst children: string = element.getAttribute('...'); // From DOM\n\n// Create React element with props\nconst componentEl = createElement(\n  Component,\n  props,                    // Plain object props\n  getChildren(children, ...) // Processed children\n);\n\n// Re-render updates: root.render() is called again with updated props\n// React diffs the vnode and updates only changed parts\nroot.render(componentEl);\n```\n\n**Props Flow:**\n1. Server renders component with props → HTML attributes\n2. HTML sent to client with attributes containing props\n3. Client parses attributes, creates React element with props\n4. On updates, component re-rendered with new props via `root.render()`\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Slots/Children Handling**\n\n#### StaticHtml Component (Wrapper for HTML content)\n```typescript\n// static-html.ts\nconst StaticHtml = ({\n  value,      // HTML string from server\n  name,       // Slot name\n  hydrate = true,\n}: {\n  value: string | null;\n  name?: string;\n  hydrate?: boolean;\n}) => {\n  if (!value) return null;\n  const tagName = hydrate ? 'astro-slot' : 'astro-static-slot';\n  return h(tagName, {\n    name,\n    suppressHydrationWarning: true,\n    dangerouslySetInnerHTML: { __html: value },\n  });\n};\n\n// Prevent React from re-rendering children\nStaticHtml.shouldComponentUpdate = () => false;\n```\n\n#### Named Slots as Props\n```typescript\n// In server.ts - named slots become props\nfor (const [key, value] of Object.entries(slotted)) {\n  const name = slotName(key); // \"my-slot\" → \"mySlot\"\n  slots[name] = React.createElement(StaticHtml, { value, name });\n}\nconst newProps = { ...props, ...slots }; // slots are props!\n```\n\n#### Default Slot as Children\n```typescript\n// In client.ts\nfunction getChildren(childString: string, experimentalReactChildren: boolean) {\n  if (experimentalReactChildren && childString) {\n    // Advanced: parse HTML children into React vnodes\n    let template = document.createElement('template');\n    template.innerHTML = childString;\n    return Array.from(template.content.children).map(createReactElementFromDOMElement);\n  } else if (childString) {\n    // Default: wrap in StaticHtml\n    return createElement(StaticHtml, { value: childString });\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n\nconst componentEl = createElement(\n  Component,\n  props,\n  getChildren(children, element.hasAttribute('data-react-children')),\n);\n```\n\n#### Example Component Usage\n```typescript\n// Counter.tsx\nexport default function Counter({\n  children,\n  count: initialCount,\n}: {\n  children: JSX.Element;\n  count: number;\n}) {\n  const [count, setCount] = useState(initialCount);\n  return (\n    <>\n      <div className=\"counter\">\n        <button onClick={() => setCount(i => i + 1)}>+</button>\n        <pre>{count}</pre>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"counter-message\">{children}</div>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n\n// Component with conditional children\nexport default function Parent({ children }) {\n  const [show, setShow] = useState(false);\n  \n  return (\n    <>\n      <input onChange={() => setShow(!show)} />\n      {show ? children : 'Nothing'}\n    </>\n  );\n}\n\n// Fragment wrapper for children passthrough\nexport default function PassesChildren({ children }) {\n  return <Fragment>{ children }</Fragment>;\n}\n```\n\n**Key Insight:** Slots flow as HTML strings from the server, wrapped in `StaticHtml` components. This prevents React from re-rendering static content (performance optimization via `shouldComponentUpdate = () => false`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. **State Management and Reactivity**\n\n#### useState (Built-in React Hooks)\n```typescript\nexport default function Counter({ count: initialCount }) {\n  const [count, setCount] = useState(initialCount);\n  const add = () => setCount((i) => i + 1);\n  const subtract = () => setCount((i) => i - 1);\n  \n  return (\n    <>\n      <button onClick={subtract}>-</button>\n      <pre>{count}</pre>\n      <button onClick={add}>+</button>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n#### Nanostores (Global Signal-like Store)\n```typescript\n// cartStore.ts\nimport { atom, map } from 'nanostores';\n\nexport const isCartOpen = atom(false);\nexport const cartItems = map<Record<string, CartItem>>({});\n\nexport function addCartItem({ id, name, imageSrc }: CartItemDisplayInfo) {\n  const existingEntry = cartItems.get()[id];\n  if (existingEntry) {\n    cartItems.setKey(id, { ...existingEntry, quantity: existingEntry.quantity + 1 });\n  } else {\n    cartItems.setKey(id, { id, name, imageSrc, quantity: 1 });\n  }\n}\n\n// CartFlyoutToggle.tsx - subscribe to store\nexport default function CartFlyoutToggle() {\n  const $isCartOpen = useStore(isCartOpen);\n  return <button onClick={() => isCartOpen.set(!$isCartOpen)}>Cart</button>;\n}\n\n// CartFlyout.tsx - derive from store\nexport default function CartFlyout() {\n  const $isCartOpen = useStore(isCartOpen);\n  const $cartItems = useStore(cartItems);\n  \n  return (\n    <aside hidden={!$isCartOpen}>\n      {Object.values($cartItems).map((cartItem) => (\n        <li key={cartItem.id}>\n          <img src={cartItem.imageSrc} alt={cartItem.name} />\n          <h3>{cartItem.name}</h3>\n          <p>Quantity: {cartItem.quantity}</p>\n        </li>\n      ))}\n    </aside>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n#### Server Actions with useActionState (React 19)\n```typescript\nimport { actions } from 'astro:actions';\nimport { useActionState } from 'react';\nimport { useFormStatus } from 'react-dom';\nimport { withState } from '@astrojs/react/actions';\n\nexport function LikeWithActionState({ postId, label, likes: initial }) {\n  const [likes, action] = useActionState(\n    withState(actions.blog.likeWithActionState),\n    { data: initial },\n  );\n\n  return (\n    <form action={action}>\n      <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"postId\" value={postId} />\n      <Button likes={likes.data} label={label} />\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction Button({likes, label}) {\n  const { pending } = useFormStatus();\n  return (\n    <button disabled={pending} type=\"submit\">\n      {likes} ❤️\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**State Patterns:**\n- **Local:** `useState()` for component state\n- **Global (Signals):** Nanostores (`atom()`, `map()`) for cross-component state\n- **Server State:** Server actions with `useActionState()` for form submissions\n\n---\n\n### 5. **SSR and Hydration Flow**\n\n#### Server-side Rendering\n```typescript\n// server.ts - Renders to HTML\nasync function renderToStaticMarkup(Component, props, { default: children, ...slotted }) {\n  const newProps = { ...props, ...slots };\n  const vnode = React.createElement(Component, newProps);\n  \n  // Choose streaming or non-streaming\n  if (opts.experimentalDisableStreaming) {\n    html = ReactDOM.renderToString(vnode); // Blocking\n  } else if ('renderToReadableStream' in ReactDOM) {\n    html = await renderToReadableStreamAsync(vnode, renderOptions); // Streaming (modern)\n  } else {\n    html = await renderToPipeableStreamAsync(vnode, renderOptions); // Streaming (legacy)\n  }\n  \n  return { html, attrs }; // HTML + props for hydration\n}\n```\n\n#### Hydration Options\n```typescript\n// client.ts\nconst renderOptions = {\n  identifierPrefix: element.getAttribute('prefix'),\n  formState,\n};\n\nconst r = hydrateRoot(element, componentEl, renderOptions as any);\n```\n\n#### Form State Preservation\n```typescript\n// Actions responses are passed via data attributes\nconst formState =\n  actionKey && actionName && stringifiedActionResult\n    ? [JSON.parse(stringifiedActionResult), actionKey, actionName]\n    : undefined;\n\n// Passed to hydrateRoot for React 19 form integration\nconst renderOptions = { formState };\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Aspect | Pattern | Technology |\n|--------|---------|------------|\n| **Mounting** | createRoot/hydrateRoot (React 18) | React DOM Client API |\n| **Props Flow** | Server attrs → Client parse → React element | Plain objects |\n| **Slots (Named)** | Props with StaticHtml wrapper | React components |\n| **Slots (Default)** | Children prop with StaticHtml | React.createElement |\n| **Local State** | useState hook | React Hooks |\n| **Global State** | atom/map signals | Nanostores |\n| **Server State** | useActionState + actions | React 19 APIs |\n| **SSR** | renderToReadableStream | React DOM Server |\n| **Unmounting** | astro:unmount event listener | Custom event |\n| **Re-renders** | root.render() with new props | Root caching (WeakMap) |\n\n---\n\n### Absolute File Paths (Reference)\n\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/client.ts` - Modern React mounting\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/client-v17.ts` - Legacy React mounting\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/server.ts` - SSR implementation\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/static-html.ts` - Slot wrapper component\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/packages/integrations/react/src/vnode-children.ts` - Children parsing utility\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/examples/with-nanostores/src/cartStore.ts` - Global state example\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro/examples/framework-react/src/components/Counter.tsx` - Component example"}],"totalDurationMs":49598,"totalTokens":41430,"totalToolUseCount":24,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":788,"cache_read_input_tokens":36643,"output_tokens":3993,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":788,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0}}}}
